  "articleBody": "Hailstorms in Texas can be incredibly destructive, and even if hail seems small, it can cause significant damage to your Aquilla home's roof. What makes hail damage so tricky is that it's often not immediately obvious from the ground. Many homeowners might not realize they have a problem until leaks appear months or even years later. Knowing what signs to look for can help you protect your home before minor issues turn into major expenses.\n\nHail damage on shingles often looks like circular dents or 'bruises' where the protective granules have been knocked off. On asphalt shingles, these impact marks expose the asphalt layer underneath, which can then be deteriorated by UV rays, leading to premature aging, cracking, and eventually, leaks. On metal roofs, hail can cause dings or dents. It's not just the roof itself; check other exterior components too. Look for dents on gutters, downspouts, siding, window frames, and even your air conditioning unit. If you see damage on these elements, it's a strong indicator that your roof likely has hail damage too. Even small hail can cause enough granule loss to compromise your roof's integrity over time. The key is that these signs aren't always dramatic; they require a careful eye, and often, a professional inspection, to detect accurately.\n\n**What to Expect During the Process**\nWhen you suspect hail damage on your Aquilla roof, a professional inspection is the critical next step. An experienced team will perform a thorough assessment, often getting up on the roof (safely, of course!) to get a close look at every shingle, flashing, and vent. They'll take detailed photos and provide clear explanations of what they find, pointing out areas of granule loss, cracks, or dents. This documentation is incredibly helpful for understanding the extent of the damage and for any potential insurance claims. They can also advise you on whether the damage is significant enough to warrant a claim or if minor repairs are a more cost-effective solution. This step-by-step guidance, from the initial inspection to understanding your options, is designed to give you peace of mind.\n\nIf you're concerned about hail damage on your Aquilla roof, schedule a professional inspection to get a clear picture of its condition.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}